<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23507" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-jūcundus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Unpleasant</i> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">minime nobis injucundus labor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fin. 1, 1, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rumor bonis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Q.
					Fr. 3, 8, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">odor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					25, 7, 36, § 74</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sonus vocis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 13, 20, 12</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">schemata,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint.
					4, 5, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">non injucundus auctor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					10, 1, 124</span></i>
			. —<i>Comp.</i>, <i><span class="en">Cael.
				Aur. Tard. 1, 4, 123</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Harsh</i>, <i>severe</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adversus malos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. Agr.
					22</span></i>
			. — <i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">injūcundē</span></b> , <i>unpleasantly</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">res injucundius actae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 1, 20, 1</span></i>
			.</div>
